Huh, really? I'm not sure any that is actually dead code so don't think it is going to be dropped. All those uniforms do get passed in and varyings getting processed. As well a lot of branching.

Or perhaps I just can't quite figure how to force this dead code elimination step. I tried a release build export with debugging off and I can't quite see any difference in the produced shader code when in live Metal debugger session.

Is there any way to have the leanest possible unlit shader in 4.5 with minimal overhead?

Interestingly, the final blit pass is also quite something. Just look at all that branching for tone mapping:

