I'm still struggling to understand what and how is going to optimise it for "real" run tbh. I'm pretty sure the GPU driver is not going to remove all of that dynamic branching based on uniforms & vertex attrs. It is surely not going to remove the branching code nor recompile the shader in the fly as the value of those uniforms can potentially change on any frame.

Despite a lot of that stuff esp in the fragment clearly doesn't belongs there when "unshaded" render_mode hint  used. E.g. the global roughness limiter logic in the fragment isn't even excluded by #ifdef MODE_UNSHADED / #endif preprocessor block. It is always there, always checked for every single pixel...    

```
...
